      instructorVoice:
        "This week we enter a critical phase of training: steelmanning. A steelman argument is the strongest, most charitable version of your opponent\u2019s position. If you can only defeat a caricature of atheism, you have defeated nothing. To truly be prepared, you must face the best arguments atheism has to offer and learn to counter them at full strength.\n\nWhy do we steelman? Because 1 Peter 3:15 commands, \u201CBut sanctify the Lord God in your hearts: and be ready always to give an answer to every man that asketh you a reason of the hope that is in you with meekness and fear.\u201D Notice: an answer to every man\u2014including the well-read, philosophically sophisticated atheist. You cannot give that answer if you have only prepared for the weakest version of their arguments.\n\nThe strongest case for atheism goes roughly like this: The universe appears to operate according to consistent natural laws. We have no reliable, repeatable, empirically verified evidence of supernatural intervention. Evolution explains the diversity of life without requiring a designer. Neuroscience increasingly explains consciousness and religious experience in physical terms. Moral behavior exists in social species without religion. And the amount of suffering in the world seems disproportionate to any loving God.\n\nThis is a formidable case. Do not underestimate it. But formidable is not irrefutable. Each of these claims contains assumptions that, when examined, reveal the need for the very God they deny. This week, we will take each steelman argument and learn to dismantle it\u2014not by mocking it, but by exposing its hidden foundations.",
