      xpReward: 131,
      instructorVoice:
        "The steelman argument from natural law runs as follows: The universe operates with remarkable consistency. Planets orbit, atoms bond, evolution proceeds\u2014all according to describable, predictable laws. We have never observed a verified violation of these laws. Therefore, positing a supernatural being who intervenes in natural processes is an unnecessary addition to our explanatory framework. Occam\u2019s Razor\u2014the principle of parsimony\u2014suggests we should not multiply causes beyond necessity.\n\nThis is a strong argument, and you must respect its force. But it has a devastating hidden assumption: it presupposes that natural laws are self-explanatory. But they are not. Why does the universe follow mathematical laws at all? Why is it intelligible? Why are the physical constants fine-tuned within incredibly narrow parameters that permit life?\n\nThe Bible answers: Colossians 1:16-17 declares, \u201CFor by him were all things created, that are in heaven, and that are in earth, visible and invisible, whether they be thrones, or dominions, or principalities, or powers: all things were created by him, and for him: And he is before all things, and by him all things consist.\u201D The word \u2018consist\u2019 (sunesteken in Greek) means \u2018hold together.\u2019 The very consistency of natural law that the atheist celebrates is the ongoing sustaining activity of Christ.\n\nAs Seventh-day Adventists, we affirm a recent six-day creation as described in Genesis 1-2 and affirmed in the fourth commandment (Exodus 20:8-11). The Sabbath itself is a weekly memorial that God is both Creator and Sustainer. The regularity of nature is not evidence against God\u2014it is evidence of His faithful, consistent character.",
      avatarPresence:
        "Your God is a god of the gaps. Every time science explains something, your God retreats. He used to cause thunder. He used to cause plagues. Now He\u2019s been pushed back to the origin of the universe\u2014and we\u2019re working on that too.\nNatural law is sufficient. Adding \u2018God\u2019 to the equation adds no explanatory power. It\u2019s like saying invisible fairies hold the planets in orbit.",
      tacticalBriefing:
        "Counter the natural law argument by shifting the question from \u2018how\u2019 to \u2018why.\u2019 Science describes how natural laws operate; it cannot explain why they exist, why they are mathematically elegant, or why they are fine-tuned for life. Also challenge the \u2018god of the gaps\u2019 accusation: we are not inserting God where we lack knowledge; we are pointing to God as the necessary foundation of the knowledge we do have.",
