      xpReward: 150,
      instructorVoice:
        "Welcome to the intermediate phase. You now have a solid doctrinal foundation against the five core atheist subjects. But intellectual arguments are only half the battle. Atheists\u2014like all skilled debaters\u2014employ psychological tactics that can disarm you if you do not recognize them. This week is about detecting and neutralizing these mind games.\n\nThe first and most common is burden shifting. The atheist will say: \u2018You believe in God\u2014you have the burden of proof. Prove He exists.\u2019 This sounds reasonable, but it is a tactical maneuver designed to put you permanently on defense while the atheist sits back and critiques.\n\nHere is the truth: everyone has a burden of proof for their worldview claims. The atheist claims the universe is self-sufficient, morality is a human invention, consciousness is a brain product, and there is no transcendent purpose. These are positive metaphysical claims that require justification. The atheist is not a neutral observer\u2014they are a committed naturalist making extraordinary claims about the nature of reality.\n\nFirst Peter 3:15 does instruct us to \u201Cbe ready always to give an answer.\u201D We gladly accept a burden of proof for our beliefs. But we must also insist that the atheist carry their own burden. Proverbs 18:17 says, \u201CHe that is first in his own cause seemeth just; but his neighbour cometh and searcheth him.\u201D Both sides must present and defend their case. Do not let the atheist play judge while you play defendant.",
      avatarPresence:
        "The burden of proof is on the one making the extraordinary claim. You\u2019re the one claiming an invisible, all-powerful being created the universe. I\u2019m simply not convinced. I don\u2019t have to prove God doesn\u2019t exist any more than I have to prove unicorns don\u2019t exist.\nUntil you meet your burden, I have no reason to take your claims seriously.",
