        "Mockery is one of the oldest rhetorical weapons, and modern atheism has elevated it to an art form. From Richard Dawkins comparing God to a \u2018Flying Spaghetti Monster\u2019 to Reddit threads ridiculing believers as delusional, the goal is the same: make faith seem so absurd that no intelligent person could hold it. If they can make you ashamed of your beliefs, they have won without engaging a single argument.\n\nThis tactic works because humans are social creatures wired for approval. Being laughed at triggers deep emotional pain. Many young Adventists abandon their faith not because they were out-argued, but because they were out-mocked. The laughter of the crowd is a powerful deterrent.\n\nBut Scripture prepares us for this. Matthew 5:11-12 records Jesus saying, \u201CBlessed are ye, when men shall revile you, and persecute you, and shall say all manner of evil against you falsely, for my sake. Rejoice, and be exceeding glad: for great is your reward in heaven: for so persecuted they the prophets which were before you.\u201D Mockery is not a new weapon\u2014the prophets faced it. Elijah was mocked. Jeremiah was mocked. Jesus Himself was mocked on the cross.\n\nSecond Peter 3:3-4 specifically warns about mockers in the last days: \u201CKnowing this first, that there shall come in the last days scoffers, walking after their own lusts, And saying, Where is the promise of his coming? for since the fathers fell asleep, all things continue as they were from the beginning of the creation.\u201D Notice: the mockers are not engaging evidence. They are using ridicule as a substitute for argument. Your job is to recognize this tactic and refuse to be moved by it.",
