        "One of the most pervasive mind games in atheist rhetoric is the narrative of progress: humanity has moved from superstition (religion) to reason (science). Faith is primitive; atheism is enlightened. Believers are on the wrong side of history. This narrative positions the atheist as intellectually evolved and the believer as a relic.\n\nThis is not an argument\u2014it is a story. And it is a false story. The founders of modern science\u2014Newton, Kepler, Boyle, Faraday, Maxwell\u2014were devout believers. The scientific method itself was born in a Christian intellectual context that assumed the universe was rationally ordered because it was created by a rational God. The \u2018Enlightenment myth\u2019 that religion and science are at war is historically inaccurate.\n\nProverbs 26:12 warns, \u201CSeest thou a man wise in his own conceit? there is more hope of a fool than of him.\u201D The false superiority complex is a form of intellectual pride that Scripture identifies as a spiritual danger. Romans 1:22 describes those who \u201CProfessing themselves to be wise, they became fools.\u201D The progressive narrative of atheism is itself a form of the very dogmatism it claims to oppose.\n\nAs SDAs, we understand history through the prophetic lens of Daniel and Revelation\u2014not through the secular myth of inevitable progress. The Bible predicts not a march toward enlightenment but a great falling away (2 Thessalonians 2:3), increasing deception (Matthew 24:24), and a final crisis before Christ\u2019s return. The \u2018progress\u2019 narrative is not just intellectually flawed; it is prophetically blind.",
